INSERT INTO "Article" ("id", "slug", "category", "country", "titleEn", "titleNe", "excerptEn", "excerptNe", "bodyEn", "bodyNe", "sources", "publishedAt", "createdAt", "updatedAt") VALUES
(gen_random_uuid(), 'periscope-labs-senior-applied-ai-engineer-dhaka-20261104', 'global', 'Bangladesh',
'AI Engineer Jobs in Dhaka: Periscope Labs Senior Applied AI Engineer Post Pays BDT 125,000-150,000, Apply by 15 November',
'',
'Periscope Labs has opened a Senior Applied AI Engineer post in Banani, Dhaka, paying BDT 125,000 to BDT 150,000 a month, with applications closing on 15 November 2026.',
'',
$$<p>Periscope Labs posted a new opening for AI engineer jobs in Dhaka on 4 November 2026, advertising a Senior Applied AI Engineer post at its Banani, Dhaka office on a full-time basis. The company said the role pays BDT 125,000 to BDT 150,000 a month, with festival bonuses and performance incentives on top, and applications close on 15 November 2026.</p>
<p>Read the experience bar before anything else, because this is a senior post with a fixed floor. Periscope Labs said applicants need at least seven years in software engineering, including at least three years in AI and machine learning and at least two years shipping large language model features to production. The post does not state how many vacancies are open, nor a remote or hybrid pattern, so applicants should not assume the role can be done from outside Dhaka. It also says nothing about visa sponsorship or work authorisation, which matters for anyone applying from outside Bangladesh.</p>
<table><tr><th>At a glance</th><th>Details</th></tr><tr><td>Employer</td><td>Periscope Labs Limited</td></tr><tr><td>Post</td><td>Senior Applied AI Engineer</td></tr><tr><td>Location</td><td>Banani, Dhaka, Bangladesh</td></tr><tr><td>Employment type</td><td>Full-time</td></tr><tr><td>Pay</td><td>BDT 125,000 to BDT 150,000 a month, plus festival bonuses and performance incentives</td></tr><tr><td>Experience required</td><td>7+ years in software engineering, including 3+ years in AI/ML and 2+ years shipping LLM features to production</td></tr><tr><td>Posted</td><td>4 November 2026</td></tr><tr><td>Application deadline</td><td>15 November 2026</td></tr><tr><td>How to apply</td><td>Email CV and LinkedIn, GitHub or portfolio to careers@periscopelabs.io with the subject line Senior Applied AI Engineer</td></tr></table>
<h2>What the Senior Applied AI Engineer role involves</h2>
<p>Periscope Labs described the post as a hands-on technical leadership role, not a ticket-taking job. The person hired will take AI work from idea to production, set the company's standards for AI quality, and mentor its AI and machine learning engineers.</p>
<p>The day-to-day work covers large language model features first: retrieval-augmented generation, semantic search, natural-language-to-SQL, and document intelligence. The engineer will also build vision and document AI, including printed and handwritten optical character recognition and vision-language models for forms, identity documents, and cheques. A further strand is agentic AI systems, which the company said must be built with human approval points, least-privilege access, and audit trails, so that automated steps stay under human control.</p>
<p>Deployment is part of the job, not an afterthought. The post lists deploying and optimising models on-premise and in the cloud using vLLM, Ollama, Hugging Face, and Triton, and running AI in production with MLOps and LLMOps practices. The engineer will build evaluation sets and track accuracy, hallucination rate, latency, and cost per request, defend systems against prompt injection and data leakage, build complete applications around AI using Cursor or Claude Code, turn customer problems into scoped features, demonstrate them to customers, and mentor engineers.</p>
<h2>Bangla AI work sits at the centre of the post</h2>
<p>One part of the posting stands out for applicants in Bangladesh. Periscope Labs said the engineer will build AI for Bangladesh, covering Bangla and Bangla-English text and speech, with quality measured in Bangla rather than judged only in English. Bangla natural language processing and speech appear again in the company's list of strong pluses, alongside handwritten OCR and vision-language models, text-to-SQL, MCP and LangGraph, fine-tuning small models, financial services experience, and mentoring.</p>
<p>That emphasis fits the company's client base. Periscope Labs said it is an ISO 9001 and ISO/IEC 27001 certified software company building enterprise platforms, analytics, and AI products for financial services, enterprise, government, and international clients, and that AI is now central to its roadmap. Applicants who have shipped Bangla language work, or document AI for forms and identity papers of the kind banks and government offices use, will be able to speak directly to the work described. The post also offers a growth path to AI Lead.</p>
<h2>Who Periscope Labs wants for this AI engineer job in Dhaka</h2>
<p>The required qualifications are specific, and applicants should check themselves against each line. Periscope Labs asked for strong Python, backend services and APIs, SQL, Git, and Docker, plus hands-on work with large language models, retrieval-augmented generation, embeddings, vector search, and structured output. It also asked for systematic AI evaluation, described as measurement rather than demonstrations that only look right, experience serving open-source models on-premise, security awareness for AI systems, and clear communication with engineers and business leaders.</p>
<p>For readers comparing routes into paid AI work, the contrast with hourly AI training work is worth noting. <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/ai-training-jobs-software-engineers-20261104">AI training jobs for software engineers</a> pay by the hour for reviewing and ranking model-written code, while this Periscope Labs post is a salaried, full-time leadership role with product ownership. Readers may also want <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/ai-startup-jobs-13514-roles-20261104">AI startup hiring across 1,100 companies</a> and <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/ai-training-jobs-consultants-20261104">AI training jobs for consultants</a>.</p>
<h2>How to apply for the Periscope Labs Senior Applied AI Engineer post</h2>
<p>Applications go by email, not through a portal. Periscope Labs said applicants should email their CV and LinkedIn, GitHub, or portfolio to careers@periscopelabs.io with the subject line Senior Applied AI Engineer. The post asks each applicant to include one AI application built end to end, setting out their own role, the architecture, and how its quality was measured. That example should match the work described, with numbers for accuracy, latency, or cost where they exist.</p>
<p>Applicants should send the email before the deadline of 15 November 2026 and keep a copy of what they sent. The post does not state a fee, a test stage, or an interview schedule, so applicants should treat anything beyond the stated email route with care. A genuine employer does not ask applicants to pay to apply, and any message asking for payment to secure this role should be treated as a fraud attempt.</p>
<h2>What to check before applying</h2>
<p>Three gaps in the posting deserve a direct check with the company before an applicant commits. First, the post does not state the number of vacancies. Second, it does not state whether any remote or hybrid working is possible, and the location given is Banani, Dhaka, so applicants outside Dhaka should ask rather than assume. Third, it does not mention notice periods, probation, or the split between on-premise and cloud work beyond the tools listed, so those points are worth raising at interview.</p>
<p>For applicants in Nepal and elsewhere in South Asia watching AI hiring in the region, the post is still a useful signal: a Dhaka software company is hiring a senior applied AI engineer specifically for Bangla language and document AI, at a stated monthly salary, with a short application window ending on 15 November 2026.</p>
<p><small>Sources: Periscope Labs Limited hiring post, published 4 November 2026 on LinkedIn, at https://www.linkedin.com/posts/periscope-labs_hiring-ai-machinelearning-activity-7523648381177606144-fa0C. The post states the role, location, pay, requirements, and application route quoted here; vacancy count, working pattern beyond full-time, and work authorisation are not stated in the post.</small></p>
$$,
'',
ARRAY['https://www.linkedin.com/posts/periscope-labs_hiring-ai-machinelearning-activity-7523648381177606144-fa0C'],
NOW(), NOW(), NOW())
ON CONFLICT ("slug") DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO "Article" ("id", "slug", "category", "country", "titleEn", "titleNe", "excerptEn", "excerptNe", "bodyEn", "bodyNe", "sources", "publishedAt", "createdAt", "updatedAt") VALUES
(gen_random_uuid(), 'bob-wms-837-posts-20261104', 'global', 'India',
'Bank of Baroda WMS Recruitment 2026: 837 Wealth Management Posts, Apply by 24 November',
'',
'Bank of Baroda has opened 837 Wealth Management Services posts on fixed-term contracts, with online applications from 4 November 2026 to 24 November 2026.',
'',
$$<p>Bank of Baroda WMS recruitment 2026 opened on 4 November 2026, with 837 posts for experienced professionals in the bank's Wealth Management Services department. The bank said online applications run from 4 November 2026 to 24 November 2026, and the recruitment is made under Advertisement No. BOB/HRM/REC/ADVT/2026/20.</p>
<p>Read the contract terms before anything else, because this is not a regular permanent bank recruitment. The bank said all 837 posts are fixed-term contractual engagements, initially for five years from joining, with a possible extension of up to five more years depending on performance and the bank's decision, and no automatic permanent appointment. The bank also said it has not published a fixed salary or cost-to-company figure for any of the five posts: pay will be set from the candidate's qualifications, experience, suitability, last-drawn salary, and market benchmarks.</p>
<table><tr><th>At a glance</th><th>Details</th></tr><tr><td>Organisation</td><td>Bank of Baroda</td></tr><tr><td>Department</td><td>Wealth Management Services (WMS)</td></tr><tr><td>Advertisement No.</td><td>BOB/HRM/REC/ADVT/2026/20, dated 4 November 2026</td></tr><tr><td>Total vacancies</td><td>837 (provisional)</td></tr><tr><td>Application window</td><td>4 November 2026 to 24 November 2026</td></tr><tr><td>Employment type</td><td>Fixed-term contract, initially 5 years, extendable by up to 5 years, maximum age 60</td></tr><tr><td>Fee</td><td>Rs. 850 for UR, EWS and OBC; Rs. 175 for SC, ST, PwBD, eligible ex-servicemen and women, plus gateway charges</td></tr><tr><td>Category split</td><td>UR 346, OBC 224, SC 124, EWS 82, ST 61; PwBD 35 horizontal, counted inside the 837</td></tr><tr><td>Preferred qualifications</td><td>Two-year full-time management postgraduate degree or diploma, MBA in Finance, Marketing or Banking, CFP, CFA or equivalent</td></tr><tr><td>Interview qualifying marks</td><td>60% for General/EWS, 55% for other reserved categories</td></tr><tr><td>Photo and signature</td><td>Photo 200 by 230 pixels, 20 to 50 KB; signature 140 by 60 pixels, 10 to 20 KB; both JPG or JPEG</td></tr><tr><td>Eligibility cut-off</td><td>1 November 2026 for age, qualification and experience</td></tr><tr><td>Age relaxation</td><td>5 years for SC/ST, 3 years for OBC non-creamy layer, higher for PwBD and eligible ex-servicemen, subject to notification conditions</td></tr><tr><td>Posting</td><td>Anywhere in India</td></tr><tr><td>Apply via</td><td>bankofbaroda.bank.in, Careers, Current Opportunities</td></tr></table>
<h2>Bank of Baroda WMS recruitment 2026: post-wise vacancies</h2>
<p>The bulk of the recruitment sits in a single post. The bank said 791 of the 837 vacancies are for Senior Relationship Manager at Deputy Manager level, followed by 35 Territory Heads, 8 Group Heads, 2 Investment Product Managers, and 1 Head Investment. The bank said the vacancy total is provisional and may change.</p>
<p>Senior Relationship Manager dominates the drive at 791 posts. The remaining posts are small and senior. Territory Head carries 35 posts, Group Head 8, Investment Product Manager 2, and Head Investment a single post. Applicants should pick one post only: the bank said that if a candidate submits more than one application, only the latest valid completed application will be retained, and fees paid for other registrations will be forfeited.</p>
<h2>Who can apply: experience is mandatory, not optional</h2>
<p>The bank said this is an experienced-professional recruitment, not a fresher drive. Senior Relationship Manager needs a graduation degree in any discipline, the prescribed NISM V-A or V-D and/or IRDA IC38 certification, and at least three years of relevant post-qualification experience as a Relationship Manager in wealth management, investment advisory, or portfolio management. Relevant experience with banks, broking firms, securities firms, and asset management companies counts, but the bank said clerical cadre experience, teaching, and training do not count, and employment periods of less than six months in one organisation are excluded.</p>
<p>The senior posts ask for more. Territory Head needs graduation and at least eight years as a Relationship Manager in the same fields, with an age limit of 28 to 42 years as on 1 November 2026. Group Head needs graduation and at least twelve years, including five years as a team lead for Relationship Managers, with an age limit of 35 to 50 years. Head Investment needs graduation with a prescribed NISM certification and at least ten years of direct investment-related work, including five years in senior leadership, with an age limit of 35 to 50 years. Investment Product Manager needs graduation with a prescribed NISM certification and at least five years, including three years as an Investment Counsellor, with an age limit of 26 to 45 years. Senior Relationship Manager has an age limit of 24 to 35 years as on 1 November 2026. Age relaxation applies by category, subject to the notification's conditions.</p>
<p>A postgraduate management qualification, an MBA, a Certified Financial Planner credential, or a Chartered Financial Analyst qualification is preferred for these posts, but the bank said it is not mandatory. Graduation alone is not enough: the prescribed professional certification and the relevant experience are mandatory.</p>
<h2>Selection, fee, and what the bank has not announced</h2>
<p>The bank said selection may include application scrutiny, an online examination, a psychometric assessment, other suitable tests, and a personal interview, as decided by the bank. It has not confirmed that every candidate will face every stage, and it has not published a question count, syllabus, duration, or marking scheme for any online examination. No examination or interview date has been announced.</p>
<p>The application fee is Rs. 850 for unreserved, Economically Weaker Section, and Other Backward Classes candidates, and Rs. 175 for Scheduled Caste, Scheduled Tribe, Persons with Benchmark Disabilities, eligible ex-servicemen, and women candidates, plus payment gateway charges. The bank said the fee is non-refundable, and is not returned even if the bank does not conduct an online examination or a candidate is not shortlisted. Fee and application must both be completed by 24 November 2026.</p>
<p>Other bank recruitment covered on this site: <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/sbi-security-officer-60-posts-20261104">SBI security officer recruitment for 60 posts</a> is open only to serving or former military and paramilitary officers, while <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/indian-bank-apprentice-1500-posts-20261104">Indian Bank apprentice recruitment for 1,500 posts</a> is a training engagement for recent graduates. Applicants may also want <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/gsssb-cce-1237-posts-20261104">GSSSB CCE recruitment for 1,237 posts</a> and <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/periscope-labs-senior-applied-ai-engineer-dhaka-20261104">Periscope Labs Senior Applied AI Engineer post in Dhaka</a>.</p>
<h2>How to apply for Bank of Baroda WMS posts</h2>
<p>Applications are online only through the bank's official website. The bank said applicants should visit bankofbaroda.bank.in, open Careers and then Current Opportunities, find Advertisement No. BOB/HRM/REC/ADVT/2026/20, and read the advertisement before applying. Applicants should then check their graduation, certification, experience, and age against the cut-off date of 1 November 2026, register, select the single post they are eligible for, upload a resume, photograph, signature, and supporting documents, and pay the fee through the online gateway by 24 November 2026.</p>
<p>Three practical points deserve attention. First, the bank said no changes will be entertained after final submission, so the form should be reviewed before submission. Second, photograph and signature specifications are tight, as listed in the table above. Third, applicants should apply only through the bank's own Careers portal and pay only through its official gateway. Bank of Baroda does not charge through agents, and any message offering a guaranteed post in this recruitment for payment is a fraud attempt.</p>
<p>The window is short, at twenty days from 4 November 2026 to 24 November 2026, so eligible wealth management professionals should not leave the application to the final day. Applicants should read the full 24-page advertisement for their chosen post before submitting.</p>
<p><small>Sources: Bank of Baroda, Advertisement No. BOB/HRM/REC/ADVT/2026/20, dated 4 November 2026, as summarised by FreeJobAlert; official portal, bankofbaroda.bank.in. Pay is not fixed in the advertisement and is described here only as the bank stated it.</small></p>
$$,
'',
ARRAY['https://www.freejobalert.com/articles/bob-recruitment-2026-senior-relationship-manager-3078340','https://bankofbaroda.bank.in'],
NOW(), NOW(), NOW())
ON CONFLICT ("slug") DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO "Article" ("id", "slug", "category", "country", "titleEn", "titleNe", "excerptEn", "excerptNe", "bodyEn", "bodyNe", "sources", "publishedAt", "createdAt", "updatedAt") VALUES
(gen_random_uuid(), 'gsssb-cce-1237-posts-20261104', 'global', 'India',
'GSSSB CCE Recruitment 2026: 1,237 Class-3 Posts, Applications Open 5 November',
'',
'Gujarat Subordinate Service Selection Board has announced 1,237 Class-3 posts through CCE 2.0, with applications opening on 5 November 2026 and closing on 30 November 2026.',
'',
$$<p>GSSSB CCE recruitment 2026 will open on 5 November 2026, with 1,237 Class-3 posts in Gujarat government departments through the Combined Competitive Examination, known as CCE 2.0. The Gujarat Subordinate Service Selection Board said applications open at 2:00 PM on 5 November 2026 and close at 11:59 PM on 30 November 2026, under Advertisement No. 468/202627 dated 3 November 2026.</p>
<p>Read the pay terms before anything else, because these are fixed-pay posts for the first five years, not regular pay-scale appointments from day one. The board said selected candidates will receive fixed monthly remuneration ranging from Rs. 26,000 to Rs. 49,600 for the first five years, depending on the post, and may become eligible for regular appointment in the corresponding government pay scale after five years of satisfactory service, subject to prevailing rules and the judicial conditions referred to in the advertisement.</p>
<table><tr><th>At a glance</th><th>Details</th></tr><tr><td>Board</td><td>Gujarat Subordinate Service Selection Board (GSSSB), Gandhinagar</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Gujarat Subordinate Services Class-3 (Group-A and Group-B) Combined Competitive Examination (CCE 2.0)</td></tr><tr><td>Advertisement No.</td><td>468/202627, dated 3 November 2026</td></tr><tr><td>Total vacancies</td><td>1,237 (Group-A 243, Group-B 994)</td></tr><tr><td>Application window</td><td>5 November 2026, 2:00 PM to 30 November 2026, 11:59 PM</td></tr><tr><td>Fee payment deadline</td><td>2 December 2026, 11:59 PM</td></tr><tr><td>Qualification</td><td>Bachelor's degree or recognised equivalent, basic computer knowledge, adequate Gujarati or Hindi knowledge</td></tr><tr><td>Age limit</td><td>20 to 35 years as on 30 November 2026, with applicable relaxation</td></tr><tr><td>Fixed pay, first 5 years</td><td>Rs. 26,000 to Rs. 49,600 a month by post</td></tr><tr><td>Reservation</td><td>Gujarat Government rules; benefits generally restricted to Gujarat recognised reserved categories</td></tr><tr><td>Preliminary exam</td><td>150 MCQs, 150 marks, 120 minutes; English 15, Gujarati 15, General Awareness and Current Affairs 30, Quantitative Aptitude 30, Reasoning 60; 0.25 negative marking per wrong answer; 40% qualifying standard</td></tr><tr><td>Apply via</td><td>ojas.gujarat.gov.in (OJAS portal)</td></tr></table>
<h2>GSSSB CCE recruitment 2026: 243 Group-A posts and 994 Junior Clerk posts</h2>
<p>Group-A holds 243 posts across eight cadres. The board said Social Welfare Inspector has the largest Group-A share at 89 posts, followed by Senior Clerk at 51 and Assistant Tribal Development Officer at 50, with Sub Registrar Grade-2 at 15, Office Assistant at 15, Head Clerk at 10, Office Superintendent at 7, and Sub Registrar Grade-1 at 6. Group-B is a single cadre: 994 Junior Clerk posts spread across Gujarat government departments and offices, led by the Commissionerate of Schools at 200 and the Commissionerate of Transport at 160. The board said the post count may increase or decrease with departmental requirements.</p>
<h2>Who can apply for GSSSB CCE 2.0</h2>
<p>The board said applicants need a Bachelor's degree or an equivalent qualification recognised by the government, basic computer knowledge, and adequate knowledge of Gujarati or Hindi. The qualification cut-off date is 30 November 2026. Computer knowledge is mandatory under the Gujarat Civil Services Classification and Recruitment (General) Rules, 1967, but the board said candidates who do not yet hold the required computer knowledge certificate may still apply, provided they obtain and produce acceptable certification before appointment.</p>
<p>The general age limit is 20 to 35 years as on 30 November 2026, before applicable relaxation. The board's summary lists five years of relaxation for general category women and for reserved category men, ten years for reserved category women subject to a maximum age of 45 years, and higher relaxation for candidates with disabilities and ex-servicemen. Applicants claiming relaxation should check the exact provision for their category in the detailed advertisement.</p>
<h2>Examination pattern: one common prelim, two different mains</h2>
<p>Group-A and Group-B candidates sit a common preliminary examination, but their main examinations differ. The board said preliminary marks are used only for screening and do not count toward final merit. The board said it will shortlist candidates for the mains separately for each group, generally up to seven times the number of category-wise vacancies.</p>
<p>The Group-A main examination is descriptive and totals 350 marks across three papers: Gujarati Language Skill at 100 marks over three hours, English Language Skill at 100 marks over three hours, and General Studies at 150 marks over three hours. The language papers cover essay writing, precis writing, comprehension, letter writing, reports, translation, and grammar. The General Studies paper covers Indian and Gujarat history, cultural heritage, the Constitution, governance, economy, geography, science, environment, and current affairs.</p>
<p>The Group-B main examination is a single objective paper of 200 marks over 120 minutes, covering the Indian State System and Constitution, Indian and State Economy and NITI Aayog, Public Administration and Governance, Discipline and Ethics in Public Service, Government Schemes, Regional, National and International Events including Current Affairs, History and Geography of Gujarat, Cultural Heritage of Gujarat, Gujarati and English, and Science, Environment and Information Technology. The board said the minimum qualifying standard of 40 per cent applies to the preliminary and main examinations, but meeting that standard does not guarantee shortlisting, since the competitive merit cut-off may be higher. No examination dates have been announced.</p>
<h2>Fee, refund, and how to apply on OJAS</h2>
<p>The preliminary examination fee is Rs. 500 for unreserved candidates and Rs. 400 for women of all categories, SEBC, Scheduled Caste, Scheduled Tribe, Economically Weaker Section, Persons with Disabilities, and ex-servicemen candidates. The board said the fee will be refunded to candidates who appear for the preliminary examination, while candidates who do not attend are not entitled to a refund. Payment is online through debit card, internet banking, UPI, or wallet on OJAS, and the fee payment deadline is 2 December 2026 at 11:59 PM.</p>
<p>Applications run through One Time Registration on OJAS, and registration alone does not count as an application. The board said applicants should complete One Time Registration if they have not already done so, select GSSSB, choose Advertisement No. 468/202627, read the complete advertisement, enter personal and educational details, complete category and reservation information, upload the prescribed photograph and signature, confirm the application, and save the confirmation number. The photograph must be in JPG format, 5 cm high by 3.6 cm wide, no larger than 15 KB, on a white background, showing the date taken, and no older than one year. The signature must be in JPG format, 2.5 cm high by 7.5 cm wide, also no larger than 15 KB. An application that has not been confirmed, or for which the mandatory fee has not been paid successfully, may not be accepted.</p>
<p>Similar drives covered on this site include <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/dsssb-delhi-court-641-posts-20261104">DSSSB recruitment for 641 Delhi court posts</a> closed on 4 November 2026, while <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/hprca-teacher-2423-posts-20261104">HPRCA teacher recruitment for 2,423 posts</a> opens on 10 November 2026. <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/bob-wms-837-posts-20261104">Bank of Baroda WMS recruitment for 837 posts</a> runs to 24 November 2026, and <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/periscope-labs-senior-applied-ai-engineer-dhaka-20261104">Periscope Labs Senior Applied AI Engineer post in Dhaka</a> closes on 15 November 2026. Applicants for GSSSB CCE 2.0 should apply only through ojas.gujarat.gov.in: no agent can secure a post, and any demand for payment outside the OJAS route should be treated as fraud.</p>
<p><small>Sources: Gujarat Subordinate Service Selection Board, Advertisement No. 468/202627, dated 3 November 2026, as summarised by FreeJobAlert; official portals, gsssb.gujarat.gov.in and ojas.gujarat.gov.in. The detailed notification is published in Gujarati; applicants should confirm post-wise and category-wise details in the full advertisement.</small></p>
$$,
'',
ARRAY['https://www.freejobalert.com/articles/gsssb-cce-2-0-recruitment-2026-3078431','https://gsssb.gujarat.gov.in','https://ojas.gujarat.gov.in'],
NOW(), NOW(), NOW())
ON CONFLICT ("slug") DO NOTHING;
